content.text:
Now tablet touch. Need implement media. Add after base or responsive. Perhaps:

```
@media (pointer: coarse) {
  .touch-controls { display:block; position:absolute; inset:0; pointer-events:none; }
  .hint-bar { display:none; }
}
@media (pointer: coarse) and (min-width: 901px) {
  .hud-bottom { bottom: max(138px, calc(env(safe-area-inset-bottom) + 130px)); }
}
```
But at 1024, map size default 143px and speed 174px, bottom 138 means map from y? screen 768: hud-bottom bottom 138, map height 143 + meta -> top ~480; touch controls bottom 18, so no overlap. Good. `drift` bottom 104, nitro 112 could overlap hud-bottom? hud-bottom at bottom 138, its top y=~480; drift y=768-104-44=620, speedo starts 768-138-174=456 to 630; drift at 620-664 overlaps speedo bottom. Hmm. On tablet, controls bottom, speedo moved up to 138 bottom = bottom edge 630, drift 620-664 overlaps. Need maybe hide drift/nitro or reposition. Better design for coarse + min-width 901:
- keep touch controls bottom 18.
- move hud-bottom bottom to 150 (bottom edge 618).
- drift bottom 104 => y 620, just below 618; okay.
